1. Create a new user account called zomatoadmin on your Linux system, and configure it so that this user can run only the apt-get update and apt-get upgrade commands using sudo without entering a password.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Edit the /etc/sudoers file using visudo and use the NOPASSWD directive for specific commands.</em>
=>useradd -m -s /bin/bash zomatoadmin
  zomatoadmin ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/apt-get update, /usr/bin/apt-get upgrade

2. Modify the sudo privileges for your existing user so that they cannot run sudo rm -rf / but can run all other sudo commands.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Use command-specific restrictions in the sudoers file to block only the dangerous command.</em>
=>ubuntu ALL=(ALL) ALL, !/bin/rm -rf /, !/usr/bin/rm -rf /, !/bin/rm -rf /*, !/usr/bin/rm -rf /*

